:name: E1M-AEN801 (Alif Ensemble E8) M55-HP smoke
:description: Boot a single Cortex-M55-HP Zephyr slice headless, no hardware.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Variables filled in by `tan renode` (tan-cli, crates/tan-core/src/
# renode.rs -> build_renode_argv).  The wrapper injects `$elf` (the
# resolved <build_dir>/zephyr/zephyr.elf), `$repl` (the platform
# descriptor) and `$vtor` (the vector-table base, derived from the ELF)
# via `renode -e "$elf=@..."` BEFORE this script runs.  The `?=`
# defaults below only apply when the variable is still unset, so the
# wrapper's values win -- and the script stays runnable by hand from an
# alp-build'd hello-world tree:
#
#     renode metadata/renode/alif_ensemble_e8.resc
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
$repl ?= @metadata/renode/alif_ensemble_e8.repl
$elf  ?= @examples/peripheral-io/hello-world/build/m55_hp-zephyr/zephyr/zephyr.elf

# Vector-table base.  Renode does NOT read this from the ELF: it guesses
# the LOWEST `vaddr` across the LOAD segments.  That is wrong for any
# image whose vector table is not in its lowest-addressed segment -- and
# an MRAM-linked Zephyr app is exactly that shape, because its `.data`
# init image has a RAM `vaddr` (0x20000000, where .data is copied TO)
# paired with an MRAM `paddr` (where the initialiser actually lives).
# Renode guesses that 0x20000000, reads SP/PC out of memory nothing was
# ever loaded into, gets zeros, and halts the CPU before executing an
# instruction (#947).
#
# The default matches the default `$elf` directly above.  hello-world
# ships no ITCM overlay, so it links per the m55_hp board .dts:
# `zephyr,code-partition = &slot0_partition`, partition@10000 of the
# MRAM -- i.e. 0x80010000 + CONFIG_ROM_START_OFFSET, which is 0 here
# because hello-world is not MCUboot-chained (the board's
# Kconfig.defconfig defaults that offset to 0x800 under
# BOOTLOADER_MCUBOOT, so a chained slot0 image links at 0x80010800
# instead).  Keep the default and the default $elf in step: a default
# that does not describe the default $elf is just a differently-wrong
# guess.
#
# Any other link shape must have $vtor passed in, and `tan renode`
# always does, computing it from the LOAD segment that CONTAINS THE
# ENTRY POINT (tan-cli#65) rather than the lowest one.
#
# IMPORTANT -- what this does and does not buy you on the pinned
# Renode v1.16.1.  Seeding VTOR fixes the HALT: Renode now reports
# `Setting initial values: PC = ..., SP = ...` from [$vtor]/[$vtor+4]
# instead of reading zeros out of unloaded memory and stopping the CPU.
# It does NOT make a high-VTOR image RUN, because of the separate
# v1.16.1 Cortex-M55 defect the .repl documents (it mis-executes a
# vector table placed at a high address like the MRAM base -- see the
# `itcm_local` block there).  Measured on v1.16.1 d66b0c2a, counting
# bus accesses after start:
#
#     ITCM-linked, $vtor=0x0             PC=0x42E1       197 accesses
#     MRAM slot0,  $vtor=0x80010000      PC=0x80010EB9     0 accesses
#     MRAM base,   $vtor=0x80000000      PC=0x80002D49     0 accesses
#
# So to actually observe a boot under this Renode pin, build the
# ITCM-linked shape (tests/renode/aen_m55_itcm_run.overlay forces
# `zephyr,flash = &itcm`, putting the vector table at the CPU-local 0x0)
# and pass `-e $vtor=0x0` for it -- the default below is the MRAM one
# and would halt that image.  The MRAM defaults here are
# correct-but-inert until the Renode pin moves past that defect.
#
# Assign it UNQUOTED -- a quoted `$vtor="0x80010000"` fails with
# `Cannot convert type 'string' to 'uint'`.
$vtor ?= 0x80010000

mach create "aen801"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl

# Surface the UART5 console.  Run headless (the wrapper passes
# `--console --disable-xwt`), so Renode routes the analyzer to stdout
# instead of a GUI window; the wrapper tees that stdout to --log, which
# is where a log-grep for the app's "[hello] done" marker would look.
# NB: no gate greps it today -- every renode workflow's boot-and-assert
# step is a no-op `echo` (#955), so nothing here is currently asserted.
showAnalyzer uart5

# Load the Zephyr ELF, then seed the vector-table base BEFORE `start`
# so Renode takes SP/PC from [$vtor] / [$vtor+4] instead of guessing.
# Order matters: `VectorTableOffset` set after `start` is too late, the
# initial values are latched when emulation begins.
sysbus LoadELF $elf
cpu VectorTableOffset $vtor

start
